#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A metaphor for distance and desire. Hands gripping the unseen weight of "
"ambition and exile.&amp;nbsp;<br/>"
msgstr ""
"Metafora za razdaljo in hrepenenje. Roke, ki oklepajo nevidno težo ambicij "
"in izgnanstva.&amp;nbsp;<br/>"

#. module: museum
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:museum.exhibitions
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A multi-artist exhibition exploring the traces of cities altered by time, "
"conflict, and migration. Through photography, video, and installation, it "
"reflects on what remains — and what is rebuilt — when a place begins to "
"disappear."
msgstr ""
"Skupinska razstava več umetnikov raziskuje sledi mest, ki so jih spremenili "
"čas, konflikti in migracije. S fotografijo, videom in instalacijo razmišlja "
"o tem, kaj ostane — in kaj se na novo zgradi — ko neki kraj začne izginjati."

#. module: museum
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:museum.exhibitions
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A room-sized kinetic sculpture made from translucent bioplastics and motion-"
"sensitive sound, reflecting the steady collapse of Arctic ice.&amp;nbsp;<br/>"
msgstr ""
"Kinetična skulptura v velikosti sobe, izdelana iz prosojne bioplastike in na "
"gibanje občutljivega zvoka, ki odseva vztrajno sesedanje arktičnega "
"ledu.&amp;nbsp;<br/>"

#. module: museum
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:museum.exhibitions
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A suspended glass and resin piece shaped like exhaled air in cold "
"temperatures; delicate and almost invisible, it addresses the fragility of "
"human and planetary breath.&amp;nbsp;<br/>"
msgstr ""
"Viseči kos iz stekla in smole, oblikovan kot izdihani zrak pri nizkih "
"temperaturah; nežen in skoraj neviden obravnava krhkost človeškega in "
"planetarnega diha.&amp;nbsp;<br/>"

#. module: museum
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:museum.exhibitions
#, fuzzy
msgid "About the artist"
msgstr "O umetniku"

#. module: museum
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:museum.homepage
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Absolutely! If a piece is not on display, you can request a private viewing "
"through our website or by visiting the museum. We'll notify you once the "
"piece is available for viewing, and you can choose to attend in person or "
"join a virtual tour. Private viewings typically take 1-2 weeks to arrange, "
"depending on availability."
msgstr ""
"Seveda! Če predmet ni razstavljen, lahko zasebni ogled zahtevate prek našega "
"spletnega mesta ali z obiskom muzeja. Obvestili vas bomo, ko bo predmet na "
"voljo za ogled, vi pa se lahko odločite, ali se boste udeležili ogleda "
"osebno ali se pridružili virtualnemu ogledu. Za organizacijo zasebnih "
